    {
      "id": "claim_2b8a799fc8724d54a32a9b81e1113ec6",
      "statement": "MultiStepFormNewProject.handleSubmit stores file bodies only for result.usedFiles (the files actually submitted to the backend) under the returned requestId but writes project.meta.json for all formData.files, and the two calls are independent, so storage is non-transactional: metadata can list artifacts whose bodies were never stored, and a mid-write failure can leave a partial directory.",
